From 01a1b53f6c0ea8fa6712ab81f07f289859465e52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:51:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 087/104] App, Unified: give new objects their localized label
 when they are added

The labels were changed after the fact by a zero timer on signalNewObject,
which also fired for restored files (renaming labels of English files and
marking them modified) and happened outside the transaction. Add
App::Document::setDefaultLabelFunction(), called in _addObject for new
objects only, and use it for the localized default labels (also for boxes,
cylinders, drawings, ...). Hiding the origin in the tree now uses the GUI's
signalNewObject instead of a timer. Remove the second, PartDesign-only way
of labeling bodies and do not overwrite the label of new sketches with the
English 'Sketch' in the integrated environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
